      "title": "The amazing health benefits of snowboarding"
    },
    {
      "type": "article-reading",
      "kicker": "Reading",
      "title": "The amazing health benefits of snowboarding",
      "article": {
        "eyebrow": "The amazing",
        "title": "health benefits of snowboarding",
        "lead": "Snowboarding is an exciting outdoor activity and is becoming very popular among teenagers. Here, we find out how it can help you to become more healthy and enjoy life more.",
        "paragraphs": [
          [
            "Taking chances is a great way to help you to have confidence in yourself – even if you don’t get it right the first time. That’s why snowboarding is a fantastic way to learn and develop a new interest. I met Kathy Champion, 15, on Mont Blanc, where she explained why snowboarding is a great ",
            {
              "text": "benefit",
              "highlight": true
            },
            " for teens."
          ],
          [
            "Kathy started snowboarding at a young age. At only nine years old, she was snowboarding with her dad in Scotland and she continues to love it to this day. (1) ",
            {
              "questionId": "read2-1"
            },
            " ‘Being in the mountains for hours every day made me feel so healthy and alive,’ she says. It helped her to understand how her body works because she learned ",
            {
              "text": "techniques",
              "highlight": true
            },
            " to help her to ride the snowboard properly. (2) ",
            {
              "questionId": "read2-2"
            },
            " ‘Snowboarding taught me to believe in myself, even when I was worried about ",
            "hurting",
            " myself.’ Did she ",
            {
              "text": "get hurt",
              "highlight": true
            },
            "? ‘Yes, once or twice, nothing serious,’ she says."
          ],
          [
            "(3) ",
            {
              "questionId": "read2-3"
            },
            " ‘It made me want to ",
            {
              "text": "succeed",
              "highlight": true
            },
            " even more and get to the bottom of the mountain!’"
          ],
          [
            "(4) ",
            {
              "questionId": "read2-4"
            },
            " ‘It keeps you very fit, very positive, but it also helps you to make new friends,’ she says. Kathy believes that doing an extreme sport also introduces you to a new and positive community. ‘To do extreme sports you need to have support from people who understand what you’re doing and are there to help you improve.’ And she thinks the feel-good part of snowboarding can also help teenagers keep out of trouble. ‘Some people I know from school laugh at me when I tell them how great I feel after snowboarding. (5) ",
            {
              "questionId": "read2-5"
            },
            "’ So, what is Kathy’s ",
            {
              "text": "advice",
              "highlight": true
            },
            "? ‘Get a snowboard, get healthy – and enjoy life!’"
          ]
        ]
      },
